# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A pretty link's brackets arrive as one token each"

# `[[` and `]]` each form ONE glyph. No outer bracket encloses a different thing from an inner
# one here, so the two halves name one mark between them: measured across 65 bundled themes,
# both halves paint identically in every one, which puts the distinction in reach of machines
# and of no theme.
#
# CANON FUSES. No grammar among twenty splits a multi-character delimiter into two separately
# named sequential tokens — VS Code html emits `</` as one token, Liquid's `{%-` as one token of
# three characters, Handlebars' `{{~{>` as one of arbitrary length — and the TextMate 1.x
# manual's own `captures` example deliberately fuses `@selector(`.
#
# THE SPLIT STANDS WHERE THE BRACKETS ENCLOSE DIFFERENT THINGS. `[img[` opens an attribute list
# and then a source; `[ext[` opens a caption and then an address. Each keeps an outer name and
# an inner name, and the cases below hold that line.

! A pretty link opens and closes on one token each

A [[Some Title]] here.
# ^^ punctuation.definition.link.begin.tiddlywiki5
# ^^ - punctuation.definition.link.inner.begin.tiddlywiki5
#             ^^ punctuation.definition.link.end.tiddlywiki5
#             ^^ - punctuation.definition.link.inner.end.tiddlywiki5

! A captioned pretty link carries the same two marks

A [[Caption|Target]] here.
# ^^ punctuation.definition.link.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                 ^^ punctuation.definition.link.end.tiddlywiki5

! An image keeps its outer and inner brackets apart

An [img width=50 [Tooltip|source.png]] here.
#  ^ punctuation.definition.image.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                ^ punctuation.definition.image.inner.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                                   ^ punctuation.definition.image.inner.end.tiddlywiki5
#                                    ^ punctuation.definition.image.outer.end.tiddlywiki5

! An external pretty link keeps its outer and inner brackets apart

An [ext[Caption|https://example.com]] here.
#  ^ punctuation.definition.link.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5
#      ^ punctuation.definition.link.external.inner.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                                  ^ punctuation.definition.link.external.inner.end.tiddlywiki5
#                                   ^ punctuation.definition.link.external.outer.end.tiddlywiki5

